\end{align}
Therefore, the variance of the normal random variable in \eqref{eq:int7} is uniformly bounded away from 0, which in turn allows one to find $\delta>0$ such that
${\Pr}(0\le\frac{\nu^{t \prime}g}{\nu^{t \prime}\tau} < \delta)\le \eta/T$.

